{"id":"b072cfa2a2eb563ab9070a55e1225ffb9ca283502c75948a3446ae49f5b0db86","lamport":1,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-11-08T20:21:42.717344668Z","format_version":1,"kind":"set-field","payload":{"fields":{"description":"## Parent\n\nSub-issue of 215ee3 (ti sync drops local-only comments, set links and deletions, and resurrects deleted tickets).\n\n## What to build\n\nA maintainer can model-check the Sync protocol. A spec of the current behaviour (key-absence Deletion, destructive Reindex) reproduces incident 215ee3 as a TLC counterexample trace. A spec of the fixed design (Deletion as an Operation, additive Reindex) passes the invariants NoLostLocalOp, NoResurrection and Convergence after a quiescent Sync. ADR 0003 \"Deletion is an operation; reindex is additive\" records the decision, the alternatives and the TLC result; ADR 0002's sync-invariant section points to it. The glossary terms Deletion, Undeletion, Reindex and Stranded index in CONTEXT.md are committed with it.\n\nAbstraction level: two clones, one remote, abstract per-ticket operation sets, delete/undelete ops, sets and lists as sets with member tombstones, git-meta merge rules as given (union; removed on one side vs modified on the other: modified wins), Reindex as \"local gains what remote has and local lacks\", push race window. No git objects, Lamport values or hashes. Not run in CI.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/spec/Sync_v0.tla` + cfg: TLC reports an invariant violation whose trace is a local delete followed by a Sync that resurrects the ticket and drops a local-only comment or link\n- [ ] `docs/spec/Sync.tla` + cfg: TLC passes NoLostLocalOp, NoResurrection, Convergence; state count recorded\n- [ ] README in docs/spec with the tla2tools command line\n- [ ] ADR 0003 written in the repo ADR format with TLC result; ADR 0002 sync section links to it\n- [ ] CONTEXT.md glossary edits committed"}}}